 "permalink": "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/2677097/can-i-free-memory-passed-to-sysallocstring",
 "body_html": "<p>When allocating a new BSTR with SysAllocString via a wchar_t* on the heap, should I then free the original wchar_t* on the heap?</p>\n\n<p>So is this the right way?</p>\n\n<pre><code>wchar_t *hs = new wchar_t[20];\n// load some wchar's into hs...\nBSTR bs = SysAllocString(hs);\ndelete[] hs;\n</code></pre>\n\n<p>Am I supposed to call delete here to free up the memory?  Or was that memory just adoped by the BSTR?</p>\n",
 "passes": [
