   "author_user_id": 123111,
   "author_display_name": "Kirill V. Lyadvinsky",
   "author_id_missing": false,
   "role": "responder",
   "is_accepted": false,
   "permalink": "https://stackoverflow.com/a/2677217",
   "score": 2,
   "created_utc": "2010-04-20T17:22:21Z",
   "last_edit_utc": null,
   "last_activity_utc": "2010-04-20T17:22:21Z",
   "license": "CC BY-SA 2.5",
   "body_html": "<p>To convert <code>wchar_t*</code> to <code>OLECHAR*</code> you need to use <a href=\"http://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/87zae4a3%28VS.80%29.aspx\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\"><code>W2OLE</code></a> macro:</p>\n\n<pre><code>wchar_t *hs = new wchar_t[20];\nUSES_CONVERSION;\nBSTR bs = SysAllocString( W2OLE(hs) );\ndelete[] hs; // no need in hs anymore since SysAllocString allocates memory\n...\n\nSysFreeString( bs );  // delete Sys string\n</code></pre>\n"
  }
